"Was living inside ponds and lakes,\nSometimes near seas with waves,\nGetting moisture, in its own ways,\nThriving thanks to the sun up and away.\n\nOn land were trees and grass,\nSurrounded by, tonnes of green mass,\nFed by the same sun, the ultimate source,\nBoth, the alga and the tree, living each day with a self-surpass!\n\nThe alga used to see the reflections\nOf the trees and the green lands above.\nPerhaps it never cared its own water,\nYet used to live in it.\n\nOne day it met a fungus on the bank,\nThey both had some similar stories,\nFormed a symbiosis, a bond strong.\nThough never connected, were now together.\n\nHelped each other.\nGot a mutual support.\nThe bond they thought will live forever.\nWell, that was a random sport.\n\nThe fungus promised,\nThey'll always be together.\nNot in like a hybrid species,\nBut a symbiosis which won't end, ever!\n\nThe alga felt something.\nThe losing grip of the fungus.\nThe fungus refused to accept it,\nPerhaps the gradual change, didn't matter.\n\nThe griped loosened a lot, one day.\nThe fungus found another alike.\nThe alga's fungus, started distancing.\nThe alga, tried to protect the symbiosis.\n\nAlga asked, what changed?\nFungus told, it found alike.\nAlga felt, drying out, and felt\nThe fungus, didn't do right.\n\nThe two fungi, formed a hyphae,\nOur alga, started returning.\nReturn to the pond, it once thrived inside.\nNow it got a lesson, that not every symbiosis, can thrive."